        <mxCell id="Rm8mzJ9XEXtdiF3RUAcq-70" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FAF9F8;strokeColor=#C8C6C4;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=16;spacingTop=10;fontSize=11;fontColor=#323130;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Design guarantees&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The NAT Gateway holds the only public IP we own - every other resource is reachable only on a private address&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Inbound lands on a private endpoint inside our VNet - the Container Apps environment has public network access disabled&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Backend runs internal ingress only - unreachable from the internet by configuration, not convention&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Every data dependency is reached through a private endpoint - each service has its public endpoint switched off&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Private DNS zones linked to the VNet resolve each service name to its 10.10.4.x address - no public resolution path&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Identity-based auth end to end - no keys or connection strings exist to leak, rotate, or audit&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;One egress point with a static IP - partners can allowlist us, outbound traffic is attributable&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="1160" x="608" y="1474.3333435058594" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Rm8mzJ9XEXtdiF3RUAcq-4" parent="1" style="image;aspect=fixed;html=1;points=[];align=center;fontSize=12;image=img/lib/azure2/networking/Virtual_Networks.svg;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="26" width="26" x="665" y="612.3333435058594" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
